Sure! Here’s a clean and tidy version of your instructions:

⸻

🛠 How to Run the Project Locally

1. 🔍 Find your local IP address

Open your terminal and run:

ifconfig

Look for the IP address under your active network (e.g., inet 10.250.197.110).
You’ll use this IP in the next steps.

⸻

2. 🚀 Start the server

Replace 10.250.197.110 with your actual IP address, then run:

PYTHONPATH="/Users/gon/Documents/Spring 2025/Data Science B/Project Pipeline" \
uvicorn backend.server:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000 \
  --ssl-keyfile=10.250.197.110-key.pem \
  --ssl-certfile=10.250.197.110.pem



⸻

3. 🌐 Open the app in your browser

On two different devices in the same network, open:
	•	https://10.250.197.110:8000/?user=A
	•	https://10.250.197.110:8000/?user=B

🔐 If prompted, accept the browser’s security warning (self-signed certificate).

⸻

